today it was announced that jager the  developer behind spec ops the line is no  longer working on Dead Island 2 Dead  Island publisher Deep Silver said in a  statement with Dead Island 2 deep silver  has always been dedicated to delivering  the sequel that dead island fans deserve  after careful consideration today we  announced the decision to part ways with  development partner jager we will  continue working towards bringing our  vision of Dead Island 2 to life and we  will share further information at a  later stage deep silver has not yet  announced which studio will be taking  over Dead Island 2 which was officially  announced during Sony's e3 press  conference last summer for playstation 4  and is also aiming to come out on xbox  one and pc the game is planned to  feature melee combat role playing game  elements and quote never-before-seen  handcrafted weapons according to Deep  Silver in Dead Island 2 which is powered  by the Unreal Engine 4 you'll visit  places like the Golden Gate Bridge in  San Francisco and Venice Beach also in  the works is multiplayer for up to eight  players in which you can quote cooperate  compete or simply coexist according to  Deep Silver will this change in  developer affect any and all of those  features planned for dead island to let  us know what you think in the comments  below and stay tuned to gamespot com /  news for all your news updates
 

